# Insights Source

Source documenting the "Insights" mental model as a conceptual tool for navigating complexity through pattern and relationship recognition. Cross-referenced with Richard H. Thaler and Cass R. Sunstein's *Nudge*.

## Source Summary

The Insights mental model is defined as a universal conceptual tool providing a mental shortcut or framework for making sense of patterns and relationships in complex situations. It is applicable across all domains with moderate confidence (0.7). The source is linked to *Nudge* by Thaler and Sunstein, which relates to choice architecture and how decisions are structured.

